cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Delegation Cascades in an Evolutionary AI Race
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/trungkiet2005/delegation-cascade"
abstract: >-
  Reproduction code for a study of what happens to a safety instruction when it
  is passed down a chain of delegated agents before anything is done with it.
  Delegation depth is made a strategic variable in the reduced AI-race game:
  each hand-off erodes the specification geometrically and each layer attenuates
  the harm attributed to the principal geometrically. Provides exact evaluation
  of the interaction layer, closed-form deniability and invasion thresholds,
  replicator and finite-population dynamics, and a comparison of four governance
  instruments.
keywords:
  - evolutionary game theory
  - replicator dynamics
  - delegation
  - principal-agent chains
  - liability
  - AI governance
  - multi-agent systems
